[{:db/id "q-64560/selection/de3f787c93c5ab9920ae5988a0d1b398cd90c00d47cb272b24263fcc095ab2a1" :answer/id #uuid "6841e37b-08c2-5d1e-944d-9189ff3037ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=1+4x+2{x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64560/selection/a063624af5896c7cf95065c233ea472c0bc8df491b11b94062b34bd6f30dab3a" :answer/id #uuid "59add6e0-6474-511a-8326-2ce46e4107d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=1+4x+2{x}^{2}-6{x}^{3}⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64560/selection/1ca0bd05eed42a0154579ac7c6114df1bdcaa5376f7ef40ce4e4039282406341" :answer/id #uuid "cb62c5d6-40c3-53a6-8427-9988a420bb22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=1-4x+{x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64560/selection/45c1d890da885d6e9c62429a44d2ab82a3948eccbe96a33f4cbef4f4fdef4c40" :answer/id #uuid "d14ee97b-9ed1-5c0b-89ea-c67522539424" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=1-4x+{x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64560/selection/cb44fb991441920c95ddbee85ef4dbd6a5af9a61effebab36eda6f32dad7be7c" :answer/id #uuid "93224542-f51e-588c-be47-2ba9602a048d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=1-4x+{x}^{2}+2{x}^{3}⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64560/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d937d908-6081-510b-bd7c-53276305a9b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64560/selection/1ca0bd05eed42a0154579ac7c6114df1bdcaa5376f7ef40ce4e4039282406341" :answer-field/choices ["q-64560/selection/de3f787c93c5ab9920ae5988a0d1b398cd90c00d47cb272b24263fcc095ab2a1" "q-64560/selection/a063624af5896c7cf95065c233ea472c0bc8df491b11b94062b34bd6f30dab3a" "q-64560/selection/1ca0bd05eed42a0154579ac7c6114df1bdcaa5376f7ef40ce4e4039282406341" "q-64560/selection/45c1d890da885d6e9c62429a44d2ab82a3948eccbe96a33f4cbef4f4fdef4c40" "q-64560/selection/cb44fb991441920c95ddbee85ef4dbd6a5af9a61effebab36eda6f32dad7be7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64560" :question/id #uuid "19930cb9-5091-5bee-a3ec-c2c2fcc00e27" :question/math-academy-id "q-64560" :question/problem "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=0$, in ascending powers of $x$ up to and including the term in ${x}^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=y+4x+{e}^{x},\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=0$:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(0)$ and ${y}^{′}(0),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{″}(0)$ and ${y}^{(3)}(0).$\n\nWe know that $y(0)=1,$ so we substitute this into the given equation to find ${y}^{″}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(0) & =y(0)+4(0)+{e}^{0} \\\\  & =1+0+1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{(3)}={y}^{′}+4+{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(0)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(0) & ={y}^{′}(0)+4+{e}^{0} \\\\  & =-4+4+1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯ \\\\  & =1+x\\cdot (-4)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}\\cdot 2+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}\\cdot 1+⋯ \\\\  & =1-4x+{x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64560/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6663cc0-4aba-5d92-b126-9c09bdac6188"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64560"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64558/selection/3a80d0fbfbaf9a22ce581865e1a6cfadac17c6274db794781a2f453f93e3116d" :answer/id #uuid "d1a977b0-ce8b-5f20-bb72-3b2d00f4b91a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-2+x-2{x}^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64558/selection/faae08a8f6ce2ae6c97cd62fbb9276632385d64d87acbe7db604db8df22d19fb" :answer/id #uuid "e53df76a-0d25-559d-a32b-58f3f5085394" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-2+x+{x}^{2}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64558/selection/12a9f1183da7e667cb91fc75545fb88151b5dbb2e0bb3badd795ec0a45bf4c1b" :answer/id #uuid "e4e4d711-bfdc-5de6-827e-fbe88992260b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-2+2x+{x}^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64558/selection/5afe6911705f47d0e98b95d80a74b43733a583341d2426d4658466b463df6205" :answer/id #uuid "67ae5b3e-6332-549f-ad05-55473cccea78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-2+2x-{x}^{2}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64558/selection/3bb25c8a4cb67a149227632f90b2cc74153d2f04110f0626e7ae60df5cae0146" :answer/id #uuid "8536aaf1-c19a-54d5-abff-949d721a4372" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-2+2x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64558/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b25b1bcb-1766-5c2f-9307-a1ca6fecf124" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64558/selection/5afe6911705f47d0e98b95d80a74b43733a583341d2426d4658466b463df6205" :answer-field/choices ["q-64558/selection/3a80d0fbfbaf9a22ce581865e1a6cfadac17c6274db794781a2f453f93e3116d" "q-64558/selection/faae08a8f6ce2ae6c97cd62fbb9276632385d64d87acbe7db604db8df22d19fb" "q-64558/selection/12a9f1183da7e667cb91fc75545fb88151b5dbb2e0bb3badd795ec0a45bf4c1b" "q-64558/selection/5afe6911705f47d0e98b95d80a74b43733a583341d2426d4658466b463df6205" "q-64558/selection/3bb25c8a4cb67a149227632f90b2cc74153d2f04110f0626e7ae60df5cae0146"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64558" :question/id #uuid "12503eb0-8f05-57ac-9a7b-e07fa7c865a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-64558" :question/problem "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=0$, in ascending powers of $x$ up to and including the term in ${x}^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=y-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,y(0)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=0$:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(0)$ and ${y}^{′}(0),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{″}(0)$ and ${y}^{(3)}(0).$\n\nWe know that $y(0)=-2,$ so we substitute this into the given equation to find ${y}^{″}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(0) & =y(0)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =-2-2(0) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{(3)}={y}^{′}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(0)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(0) & ={y}^{′}(0)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2-2(1) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinaly, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯ \\\\ y(x) & =-2+x\\cdot 2+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}\\cdot (-2)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}\\cdot 0+⋯ \\\\ y(x) & =-2+2x-{x}^{2}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64558/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6663cc0-4aba-5d92-b126-9c09bdac6188"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64558"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79943/selection/a77accc4f89a6c3850f9d2195818a4c7ad5907f3f91d1a9de1a3ad8c6aaadbbf" :answer/id #uuid "8b1f4bfd-85e4-5fb2-90d0-8b932b0081a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2+2x-5{x}^{2}+\\frac{5{x}^{3}}{3}⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79943/selection/9ae710b1bdbfab29c39ac3ee966100c9bd87a561101c2958aa8b75b3af5fe013" :answer/id #uuid "f304219a-51d4-52ad-bda6-a8685241e295" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2+2x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79943/selection/30f1cfc3d56432400b76b927f408e94d81e9224d28130d3102dbfe670cbb7e92" :answer/id #uuid "1b087f52-71b0-5293-8de1-7b40401edddb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2+2x-5{x}^{2}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79943/selection/35931f9d3e76177436dec20b52c07e21a0cb881259c90e4d9d601371760e3734" :answer/id #uuid "dac0eecf-dc61-5ed9-8688-9170e6d6afe3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2+2x+2{x}^{2}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79943/selection/366fa51a95861c34613b35cc6e65db9100f561c86b4bdeed26319b6c2c4f034d" :answer/id #uuid "094d2f16-5806-56a0-8c0b-d0d00df61fd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2+2x+\\frac{5{x}^{3}}{3}⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79943/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3eb5ed3b-8a6d-51bd-a72b-b2a59f0e3cbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79943/selection/30f1cfc3d56432400b76b927f408e94d81e9224d28130d3102dbfe670cbb7e92" :answer-field/choices ["q-79943/selection/a77accc4f89a6c3850f9d2195818a4c7ad5907f3f91d1a9de1a3ad8c6aaadbbf" "q-79943/selection/9ae710b1bdbfab29c39ac3ee966100c9bd87a561101c2958aa8b75b3af5fe013" "q-79943/selection/30f1cfc3d56432400b76b927f408e94d81e9224d28130d3102dbfe670cbb7e92" "q-79943/selection/35931f9d3e76177436dec20b52c07e21a0cb881259c90e4d9d601371760e3734" "q-79943/selection/366fa51a95861c34613b35cc6e65db9100f561c86b4bdeed26319b6c2c4f034d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79943" :question/id #uuid "4746f966-cd54-53d0-932c-4e65b0d67e06" :question/math-academy-id "q-79943" :question/problem "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=0$, in ascending powers of $x$ up to and including the term in ${x}^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=2y-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,y(0)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=0$:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(0)$ and ${y}^{′}(0),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{″}(0)$ and ${y}^{(3)}(0).$\n\nWe know that $y(0)=-2,$ so we substitute this into the given equation to find ${y}^{″}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(0) & =2y(0)-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =2(-2)-6(1) \\\\  & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{(3)}=2{y}^{′}+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(0)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(0) & =2{y}^{′}(0)+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2(2)+0 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinaly, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯ \\\\ y(x) & =-2+x\\cdot 2+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}\\cdot (-10)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}\\cdot 4+⋯ \\\\ y(x) & =-2+2x-5{x}^{2}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79943/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6663cc0-4aba-5d92-b126-9c09bdac6188"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79943"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64557/selection/117dacede8c1a6b30511f7e79c796d8ec9d19d978c57c08d7dfca4ac02c18881" :answer/id #uuid "50d7005c-4d6b-5cfc-9f60-359e516e729f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-2-3{x}^{2}+\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64557/selection/31b8b58c340083d9438d6ad93bd3993058ad37fc81e71f819c0868f314824ee0" :answer/id #uuid "b40d0424-0c4d-56a5-a5ea-16c1a542755b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-2-{x}^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64557/selection/e139fd23c6fa57ea495dd2e48d2ec460fe63fe8cf3ab64bc06ac55e510beb6e2" :answer/id #uuid "2b83db21-4b99-590c-a33c-4ccb6b4cc17c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-2+3{x}^{2}+\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64557/selection/75f1fff9bff1dc938dcca8296e44f10d5378dafca530b77ffbb60a5108cea36a" :answer/id #uuid "8aadaa9e-1a5d-5225-b018-d25de1092245" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-2-{x}^{2}+\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64557/selection/3d6e63db650a74196c514864a11b550ed1acef1a7030b455bee6c99c59316019" :answer/id #uuid "f1e75c75-2d1c-5c9f-8a33-963e06b1b0df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-2+{x}^{2}-\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64557/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d228d5a4-b262-5f38-88e9-553b7d3a77b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64557/selection/75f1fff9bff1dc938dcca8296e44f10d5378dafca530b77ffbb60a5108cea36a" :answer-field/choices ["q-64557/selection/117dacede8c1a6b30511f7e79c796d8ec9d19d978c57c08d7dfca4ac02c18881" "q-64557/selection/31b8b58c340083d9438d6ad93bd3993058ad37fc81e71f819c0868f314824ee0" "q-64557/selection/e139fd23c6fa57ea495dd2e48d2ec460fe63fe8cf3ab64bc06ac55e510beb6e2" "q-64557/selection/75f1fff9bff1dc938dcca8296e44f10d5378dafca530b77ffbb60a5108cea36a" "q-64557/selection/3d6e63db650a74196c514864a11b550ed1acef1a7030b455bee6c99c59316019"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64557" :question/id #uuid "3d1d32a0-6249-5ad9-baca-e7fe99dac145" :question/math-academy-id "q-64557" :question/problem "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=0$, in ascending powers of $x$ up to and including the term in ${x}^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=3y+4{e}^{2x},\\,y(0)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=0$:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(0)$ and ${y}^{′}(0),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{″}(0)$ and ${y}^{(3)}(0).$\n\nWe know that $y(0)=-2,$ so we substitute this into the given equation to find ${y}^{″}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(0) & =3y(0)+4{e}^{2(0)} \\\\  & =3(-2)+4(1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{(3)}=3{y}^{′}+8{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(0)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(0) & =3{y}^{′}(0)+8{e}^{2(0)} \\\\  & =3(0)+8 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinaly, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯ \\\\  & =-2+x\\cdot 0+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}\\cdot (-2)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}\\cdot 8+⋯ \\\\  & =-2-{x}^{2}+\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64557/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6663cc0-4aba-5d92-b126-9c09bdac6188"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64557"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64503"] :question/problem "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=0$, in ascending powers of $x$ up to and including the term in ${x}^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=y+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\,y(0)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=0$:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(0)$ and ${y}^{′}(0),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{″}(0)$ and ${y}^{(3)}(0).$\n\nWe know that $y(0)=-1,$ so we substitute this into the given equation to find ${y}^{″}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(0) & =y(0)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0) \\\\  & =-1+2 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{(3)}={y}^{′}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(0)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(0) & ={y}^{′}(0)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =-0-0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯ \\\\  & =-1+x\\cdot 0+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}\\cdot 1+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}\\cdot 0+⋯ \\\\  & =-1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-79947/selection/e8c3ad8fbfbf59b866b2ac712f39fc248e25af637474004c5d42782d61115d85" :answer/id #uuid "2dc4bc49-8fbb-56fd-aedc-6bea9b61b668" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2+(x-1)-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79947/selection/a2bd3dc8b2df8aad8a59d16a97ce0a06d3efa526c09e3d05ff3436a26224091f" :answer/id #uuid "91c292d2-a83e-50e9-8751-0cd620433639" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2-(x-1)-\\frac{3(x-1)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{5}{6}(x-1)^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79947/selection/c6d76224b4e97e53e0494a906d47a2f3069352fb6680adc71b66bf9179a93f6e" :answer/id #uuid "b9de4032-d6f6-5d7b-b2ec-ca0de85a51f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2+(x-1)+\\frac{3(x-1)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79947/selection/d6c643e814b5d6a5a484c89722df149e31539744387124453bd739d1c652496a" :answer/id #uuid "010f9b90-e505-581b-b2a2-e4e6ba9cc1df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2+(x-1)-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{5}{6}(x-1)^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79947/selection/7d0bd2445417ca189ab11a8e6ef51d6a0e182fd8c6e9c69f66590fe05502e8c8" :answer/id #uuid "91b3900c-1aab-59d0-9112-ae39247f3529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2+(x-1)-\\frac{3(x-1)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{7}{6}(x-1)^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79947/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "535ec008-1a7c-5e26-a2ea-df95bcae8dee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79947/selection/d6c643e814b5d6a5a484c89722df149e31539744387124453bd739d1c652496a" :answer-field/choices ["q-79947/selection/e8c3ad8fbfbf59b866b2ac712f39fc248e25af637474004c5d42782d61115d85" "q-79947/selection/a2bd3dc8b2df8aad8a59d16a97ce0a06d3efa526c09e3d05ff3436a26224091f" "q-79947/selection/c6d76224b4e97e53e0494a906d47a2f3069352fb6680adc71b66bf9179a93f6e" "q-79947/selection/d6c643e814b5d6a5a484c89722df149e31539744387124453bd739d1c652496a" "q-79947/selection/7d0bd2445417ca189ab11a8e6ef51d6a0e182fd8c6e9c69f66590fe05502e8c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79947" :question/id #uuid "6545ba2b-d4b7-5ea7-b830-ebbd2f1300c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-79947" :question/problem "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=1$, in ascending powers of $(x-1)$ up to and including the term in $(x-1)^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{′},\\,y(1)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=1$:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(1)+(x-1){y}^{′}(1)+\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(1)+\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(1)+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(1)$ and ${y}^{′}(1),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{″}(1)$ and ${y}^{(3)}(1).$\n\nWe substitute $y(1)=2$ and ${y}^{′}(1)=1$ into the given equation to find ${y}^{″}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(1) & ={y}^{2}(1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-{y}^{′}(1) \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 0-1 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{(3)}(x)=2y{y}^{′}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}-{y}^{″}\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(1)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(1) & =2y(1){y}^{′}(1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{{y}^{2}(1)}{1}-{y}^{″}(1) \\\\  & =2(2)(1)(0)+\\frac{(2)^{2}}{1}-(-1) \\\\  & =4+1 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinaly, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(1)+(x-1){y}^{′}(1)+\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(1)+\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(1)+⋯ \\\\  & =2+(x-1)\\cdot 1+\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}\\cdot (-1)+\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{6}\\cdot 5+… \\\\  & =2+(x-1)-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{5}{6}(x-1)^{3}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79947/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7aa5350-6bfc-5057-ad4a-3bd97a31da5e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79947"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79945/selection/4a62e499188b18189d5c98fb6c84c750a8cea578d608efcd563eae7593aebfd5" :answer/id #uuid "eea87caf-0a47-5bbd-a9ab-f91ff53deda6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1-(x-\\pi )+\\frac{1}{3}(x-\\pi )^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79945/selection/d1f1d8965eecfef09ef15c57541ce976886f0d3cb09c4b1fa89403439e1bb3c7" :answer/id #uuid "e7c55260-f88d-5a60-9b44-07745eee8c2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1-(x-\\pi )-\\frac{1}{6}(x-\\pi )^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79945/selection/0f38c724da2cda0724260248a76d409e8e389fadded3881809650089439ca4c4" :answer/id #uuid "14202016-ee18-572b-828c-02f3bd7d449e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1+(x-\\pi )+\\frac{1}{3}(x-\\pi )^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79945/selection/c95faf9049c3daea00037799be3b372dc3bd50e430cf0afd359cb45d4cc7edc4" :answer/id #uuid "3da490db-66a7-5550-9449-e62ea05e7e0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1+(x-\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\pi )^{2}-\\frac{1}{9}(x-\\pi )^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79945/selection/a770f4622be27ceb1bfd560aac163023faca76498a5b722920557944aa9bdbf9" :answer/id #uuid "c8ceca87-fbb1-56cb-bd77-0d6e0c7803fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1-(x-\\pi )-\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\pi )^{3}+\\frac{1}{3}(x-\\pi )^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79945/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e7f0da5-8e95-52a0-875d-257a7ff4b87e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79945/selection/d1f1d8965eecfef09ef15c57541ce976886f0d3cb09c4b1fa89403439e1bb3c7" :answer-field/choices ["q-79945/selection/4a62e499188b18189d5c98fb6c84c750a8cea578d608efcd563eae7593aebfd5" "q-79945/selection/d1f1d8965eecfef09ef15c57541ce976886f0d3cb09c4b1fa89403439e1bb3c7" "q-79945/selection/0f38c724da2cda0724260248a76d409e8e389fadded3881809650089439ca4c4" "q-79945/selection/c95faf9049c3daea00037799be3b372dc3bd50e430cf0afd359cb45d4cc7edc4" "q-79945/selection/a770f4622be27ceb1bfd560aac163023faca76498a5b722920557944aa9bdbf9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79945" :question/id #uuid "f2480529-9e51-5e8c-9f4c-f59546697173" :question/math-academy-id "q-79945" :question/problem "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=\\pi $, in ascending powers of $(x-\\pi )$ up to and including the term in $(x-\\pi )^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,y(\\pi )=1,\\,{y}^{′}(\\pi )=-1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=\\pi $:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(\\pi )+(x-\\pi ){y}^{′}(\\pi )+\\frac{(x-\\pi )^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(\\pi )+\\frac{(x-\\pi )^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(\\pi )+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(\\pi )$ and ${y}^{′}(\\pi ),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{″}(\\pi )$ and ${y}^{(3)}(\\pi ).$\n\nWe substitute $y(\\pi )=1$ into the given equation to find ${y}^{″}(\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(\\pi ) & ={y}^{2}(\\pi )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & ={1}^{2}\\cdot (0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{(3)}(x)=2y{y}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(\\pi )$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(\\pi ) & =2y(\\pi ){y}^{′}(\\pi )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+{y}^{2}(\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =2(1)(-1)(0)+(1)^{2}(-1) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(\\pi )+(x-\\pi ){y}^{′}(\\pi )+\\frac{(x-\\pi )^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(\\pi )+\\frac{(x-\\pi )^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(\\pi )+⋯ \\\\  & =1+(x-\\pi )\\cdot (-1)+\\frac{(x-\\pi )^{2}}{2}\\cdot (0)+\\frac{(x-\\pi )^{3}}{6}\\cdot (-1)+… \\\\  & =1-(x-\\pi )-\\frac{1}{6}(x-\\pi )^{3}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79945/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7aa5350-6bfc-5057-ad4a-3bd97a31da5e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79945"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64563/selection/ea867029aa4255e5887e55693cdc453d8190df69b96b87325330fd2ccb2e4e45" :answer/id #uuid "5b4b979d-380a-5124-a2cd-06373c377d0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=3+\\frac{3}{2}(x+1)^{2}+(x+1)^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64563/selection/0ecc41d27135b262a1d0599d86375043154d565bc219606ed5edfaa0893e5092" :answer/id #uuid "f83008cd-22dc-5d4c-93a2-91ba1fabe532" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=3-\\frac{1}{2}(x+1)^{2}-(x+1)^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64563/selection/7fee29c6cb42f22f7ac8fd72672b6d5d46d8e9c677a1d9cadbcffc03d115ac4b" :answer/id #uuid "72291c81-8a00-58e8-85a4-f85c913996e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=3+\\frac{3}{2}(x+1)^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}(x+1)^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64563/selection/beafee088c45585b5c92c3b43423ca58d462187b5f3ae92f44531abec6669cab" :answer/id #uuid "d6c88f54-421e-56f9-816c-ef22701cf4fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=3-\\frac{1}{2}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(x+1)^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64563/selection/1cb7e31a4dbf0c42144e37bde10850f1085980faea03492ee962479ce4ff0287" :answer/id #uuid "98a91770-d6b3-560b-9fcf-ccdfde90a1c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=3+\\frac{3}{2}(x+1)^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}(x+1)^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64563/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e88a28f-99ed-5483-8e06-11db7bb3ba34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64563/selection/1cb7e31a4dbf0c42144e37bde10850f1085980faea03492ee962479ce4ff0287" :answer-field/choices ["q-64563/selection/ea867029aa4255e5887e55693cdc453d8190df69b96b87325330fd2ccb2e4e45" "q-64563/selection/0ecc41d27135b262a1d0599d86375043154d565bc219606ed5edfaa0893e5092" "q-64563/selection/7fee29c6cb42f22f7ac8fd72672b6d5d46d8e9c677a1d9cadbcffc03d115ac4b" "q-64563/selection/beafee088c45585b5c92c3b43423ca58d462187b5f3ae92f44531abec6669cab" "q-64563/selection/1cb7e31a4dbf0c42144e37bde10850f1085980faea03492ee962479ce4ff0287"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64563" :question/id #uuid "01287eda-c6af-5470-b60e-fc0a3ea0e31c" :question/math-academy-id "q-64563" :question/problem "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=-1$, in ascending powers of $(x+1)$ up to and including the term in $(x+1)^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}={x}^{2}y-{y}^{′},\\,y(-1)=3,\\,{y}^{′}(-1)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=-1$:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(-1)+(x+1){y}^{′}(-1)+\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(-1)+\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(-1)+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(-1)$ and ${y}^{′}(-1),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{″}(-1)$ and ${y}^{(3)}(-1).$\n\nWe substitute $y(-1)=3$ and ${y}^{′}(-1)=0$ into the given equation to find ${y}^{″}(-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(-1) & =(-1)^{2}y(-1)-{y}^{′}(-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 3-0 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{(3)}(x)=2xy+{x}^{2}{y}^{′}-{y}^{″}\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(-1)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(-1) & =2(-1)y(-1)+(-1)^{2}{y}^{′}(-1)-{y}^{″}(-1) \\\\  & =(2\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 3)+((-1)^{2}\\cdot 0)-3 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(-1)+(x+1){y}^{′}(-1)+\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(-1)+\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(-1)+⋯ \\\\  & =3+(x+1)\\cdot 0+\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{2}\\cdot 3+\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{6}\\cdot (-9)+… \\\\  & =3+\\frac{3}{2}(x+1)^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}(x+1)^{3}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-64563/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7aa5350-6bfc-5057-ad4a-3bd97a31da5e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64563"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64504"] :question/problem "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=1$, in ascending powers of $(x-1)$ up to and including the term in $(x-1)^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=xy+{y}^{′},\\,y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=1$:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(1)+(x-1){y}^{′}(1)+\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(1)+\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(1)+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(1)$ and ${y}^{′}(1),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{″}(1)$ and ${y}^{(3)}(1).$\n\nWe substitute $y(1)=1$ and ${y}^{′}(1)=2$ into the given equation to find ${y}^{″}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(1) & =1\\cdot y(1)+{y}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{(3)}(x)=x{y}^{′}+y+{y}^{″}\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(1)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(1) & =1\\cdot {y}^{′}(1)+y(1)+{y}^{″}(1) \\\\  & =2+1+3 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(1)+(x-1){y}^{′}(1)+\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(1)+\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(1)+⋯ \\\\  & =1+(x-1)\\cdot 2+\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}\\cdot 3+\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{6}\\cdot 6+… \\\\  & =1+2(x-1)+\\frac{3}{2}(x-1)^{2}+(x-1)^{3}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-79946/selection/bce22bf412698ade595bb6b2b75223dd1cfccaae9fdfedaf935d8d2e0dd1e9f0" :answer/id #uuid "10f674bf-70dd-5a67-98d8-5507caec4067" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+2(x-2)-2(x-2)^{2}-\\frac{(x-2)^{3}}{2}+…" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79946/selection/9bfd86bf86b30ed85382c3ab93833d04959c2131a4b16c517e262dee812e6d4b" :answer/id #uuid "34509396-6013-5728-af44-849fc65b3dc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+2(x-2)+(x-2)^{2}-2(x-2)^{3}+…" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79946/selection/23bebcf3ba3a3c33ecc5fd4e16b11a0f7bcf227c7fa5dde21ccf49833064f9b1" :answer/id #uuid "96454422-3748-5075-87d5-9e97300ec889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+2(x-2)-(x-2)^{2}+2(x-2)^{3}+…" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79946/selection/34cc9431d14def471528c890ec06236d10c0ac68f8c13aed0e2327b18d85fad1" :answer/id #uuid "c79a374f-a1a8-55de-abc7-9551de0a2000" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+2(x-2)+2(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{(x-2)^{3}}{2}+…" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79946/selection/356528997816543d20c9c022cb353b8cdf5163e2d8693f2a5c406bba817a701f" :answer/id #uuid "781ff251-58d7-59b2-8c5b-fed562a2c0a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+2(x-2)-(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{(x-2)^{3}}{2}+…" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79946/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "52bccafb-2974-57c8-831c-4a9ddeb90fdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79946/selection/356528997816543d20c9c022cb353b8cdf5163e2d8693f2a5c406bba817a701f" :answer-field/choices ["q-79946/selection/bce22bf412698ade595bb6b2b75223dd1cfccaae9fdfedaf935d8d2e0dd1e9f0" "q-79946/selection/9bfd86bf86b30ed85382c3ab93833d04959c2131a4b16c517e262dee812e6d4b" "q-79946/selection/23bebcf3ba3a3c33ecc5fd4e16b11a0f7bcf227c7fa5dde21ccf49833064f9b1" "q-79946/selection/34cc9431d14def471528c890ec06236d10c0ac68f8c13aed0e2327b18d85fad1" "q-79946/selection/356528997816543d20c9c022cb353b8cdf5163e2d8693f2a5c406bba817a701f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79946" :question/id #uuid "780e5b34-23c5-5a8d-b25c-b06e158f186e" :question/math-academy-id "q-79946" :question/problem "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=2$, in ascending powers of $(x-2)$ up to and including the term in $(x-2)^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=y-{e}^{2-x},\\,y(2)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=2$:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(2)+(x-2){y}^{′}(2)+\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(2)+\\frac{(x-2)^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(2)+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(2)$ and ${y}^{′}(2),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{″}(2)$ and ${y}^{(3)}(2).$\n\nWe substitute $y(2)=-1$ into the given equation to find ${y}^{″}(2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(2) & =y(2)-{e}^{2-2} \\\\  & =-1-{e}^{0} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{(3)}(x)={y}^{′}+{e}^{2-x}\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(1)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(2) & ={y}^{′}(2)+{e}^{2-2} \\\\  & =2+{e}^{2-2} \\\\  & =2+{e}^{0} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(2)+(x-2){y}^{′}(2)+\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(2)+\\frac{(x-2)^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(2)+⋯ \\\\  & =-1+(x-2)\\cdot (2)+\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}\\cdot (-2)+\\frac{(x-2)^{3}}{6}\\cdot 3+… \\\\  & =-1+2(x-2)-(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{(x-2)^{3}}{2}+…\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79946/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7aa5350-6bfc-5057-ad4a-3bd97a31da5e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79946"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64565/selection/c297fe7b8a4aee15198f07ad4b4a5bebaf6675ae3ffb5b9709f8b3b26fa24f72" :answer/id #uuid "36e03b02-db4a-5062-a76b-51dfb2ebcf83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-1-x+{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64565/selection/e191597ab878f60d32e8dde342f681083175b718f75ab4d51a516704908498a6" :answer/id #uuid "d37f23e5-bef3-5714-be48-da4d77b65aca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-1+x+{x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64565/selection/5331d5d3518d85ac879557053e0e7c6ad2d2f9a4302e7931f881477545bb04ce" :answer/id #uuid "4d888476-7d8f-5471-84f3-f6bab95d537d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-1-x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64565/selection/e667045c7bcaafbc4b614e94b5b1ffe7ec21f74b6e02e004222e194f336ae60e" :answer/id #uuid "38d34739-a950-5ff2-919a-085a3b2f17a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-1+x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64565/selection/59fd24503ca3df64e54df14c70a99b9559f027f261f771a0aef77094b579dcb7" :answer/id #uuid "73693f81-66ed-57b7-a206-67fd7921a257" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-1+x-\\frac{5{x}^{3}}{6}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64565/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "37e8dac8-6600-5820-b99a-85a6e827910d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64565/selection/e667045c7bcaafbc4b614e94b5b1ffe7ec21f74b6e02e004222e194f336ae60e" :answer-field/choices ["q-64565/selection/c297fe7b8a4aee15198f07ad4b4a5bebaf6675ae3ffb5b9709f8b3b26fa24f72" "q-64565/selection/e191597ab878f60d32e8dde342f681083175b718f75ab4d51a516704908498a6" "q-64565/selection/5331d5d3518d85ac879557053e0e7c6ad2d2f9a4302e7931f881477545bb04ce" "q-64565/selection/e667045c7bcaafbc4b614e94b5b1ffe7ec21f74b6e02e004222e194f336ae60e" "q-64565/selection/59fd24503ca3df64e54df14c70a99b9559f027f261f771a0aef77094b579dcb7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64565" :question/id #uuid "021705db-d582-5e99-9214-2d24aeb3b8f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-64565" :question/problem "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=0$, in ascending powers of $x$ up to and including the term in ${x}^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-y{e}^{x},\\,y(0)=-1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=0$:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(0),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{′}(0),$  ${y}^{″}(0)$ and ${y}^{(3)}(0).$\n\nWe know that $y(0)=-1,$ so we substitute this into the given equation to find ${y}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(0) & =(0)^{2}-y(0){e}^{0} \\\\  & =0-(-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{″}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)=2x-{y}^{′}{e}^{x}-y{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{″}(0)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(0) & =2(0)-{y}^{′}(0){e}^{0}-y(0){e}^{0} \\\\  & =0-(1\\cdot 1)-(-1\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate ${y}^{″}(x)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(x) & =2-{y}^{″}{e}^{x}-2{y}^{′}{e}^{x}-y{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(0)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(0) & =2-{y}^{″}(0){e}^{0}-2{y}^{′}(0){e}^{0}-y(0){e}^{0} \\\\  & =2-(0\\cdot 1)-(2\\cdot 1\\cdot 1)-((-1)\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =2-0-2+1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯ \\\\  & =-1+x\\cdot (1)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\cdot 0+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}\\cdot 1+⋯ \\\\  & =-1+x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-64565/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f407cd0-11c1-59c6-a7c5-25e4be37e2d5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64565"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79951/selection/10d42ce847208af9cc45b49255f64ce56fc52f200ec58673f273b18a05ce1e42" :answer/id #uuid "9812009e-351c-598e-bb1c-c24b5e1ea0d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+x-{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79951/selection/d2c7b7d66d0b56bb92f13016dcff48409301eff3389073077cbb16d4fbc465da" :answer/id #uuid "12cbb1f9-a8fd-5aa7-9087-7fb3c6d5dcb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79951/selection/f1d5c5d5e7f32a145fe967072611e069a78d6c44989937c2c550fc53bad8516a" :answer/id #uuid "e91064c1-d2a7-5bbb-b2d5-bb2324582401" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+2x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79951/selection/c75c1b717f5cc92aa72e166d8f3c0c3ba9d47dfb815ba28744793dcf3988997f" :answer/id #uuid "bfd3bd69-c0bd-5092-9697-83b7186f1f68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+2x+{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79951/selection/15d2e0e893cd17dca33d717b1e59ad4c84a50bcc89b155c60ce3beebae2a9f4e" :answer/id #uuid "9b099422-7bcd-5d70-906f-ee036542a79a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{3}}{6}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79951/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "83a22fab-ae8d-5f61-b572-db8e645c3764" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79951/selection/d2c7b7d66d0b56bb92f13016dcff48409301eff3389073077cbb16d4fbc465da" :answer-field/choices ["q-79951/selection/10d42ce847208af9cc45b49255f64ce56fc52f200ec58673f273b18a05ce1e42" "q-79951/selection/d2c7b7d66d0b56bb92f13016dcff48409301eff3389073077cbb16d4fbc465da" "q-79951/selection/f1d5c5d5e7f32a145fe967072611e069a78d6c44989937c2c550fc53bad8516a" "q-79951/selection/c75c1b717f5cc92aa72e166d8f3c0c3ba9d47dfb815ba28744793dcf3988997f" "q-79951/selection/15d2e0e893cd17dca33d717b1e59ad4c84a50bcc89b155c60ce3beebae2a9f4e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79951" :question/id #uuid "13dde15f-53dc-52e9-8781-7f7c083b83f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-79951" :question/problem "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=0$, in ascending powers of $x$ up to and including the term in ${x}^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,y(0)=-1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=0$:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(0),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{′}(0),$  ${y}^{″}(0)$ and ${y}^{(3)}(0).$\n\nWe know that $y(0)=-1,$ so we substitute this into the given equation to find ${y}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(0) & =2(0)-y(0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{″}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)=2-{y}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{″}(0)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(0) & =2-{y}^{′}(0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+y(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =2-(1)(1)+(-1)(0) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate ${y}^{″}(x)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{(3)}(x)=-{y}^{″}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{y}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{y}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-{y}^{″}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2{y}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(0)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(0) & =-{y}^{″}(0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+2{y}^{′}(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+y(0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =-(1)(1)+2(1)(0)+(-1)(1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯ \\\\  & =-1+x\\cdot 1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\cdot 1+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}\\cdot (-2)+⋯ \\\\  & =-1+x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-79951/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f407cd0-11c1-59c6-a7c5-25e4be37e2d5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79951"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79953/selection/29ae03a9f761d292abc2b5d20a15cc24e1ef327068213c1dd84fce3312e3b7eb" :answer/id #uuid "03e8caea-a558-5acb-8d77-2b2a47abc249" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79953/selection/737b3859a1677c2f6ae68e264efcac758d99acb897ef54b6b3acffe10b8cc375" :answer/id #uuid "bd6c98c8-1007-5180-939a-e41abb957684" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+x+{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79953/selection/eeead72e2dd6a2e09614677b57e63b777fbc709ff8634de9726490c4bbb38b6f" :answer/id #uuid "e24f2be1-adb7-54f6-8266-9efd6716570f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79953/selection/537de86f0ed48c4ed4b80f03e49ca3bf9e07200cc99d1325a778ee3c52e95a9b" :answer/id #uuid "ba31a88d-2484-5205-911f-cdc1d7ff3297" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79953/selection/e4f339ecf183451e92410984586abe05eb379f62474adfa47a4381e3cf60f2aa" :answer/id #uuid "1ef3f159-a0ab-53bd-87cd-16f583839189" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1+x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79953/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "00f75621-42e2-5cf2-989f-3c2c999d28fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79953/selection/eeead72e2dd6a2e09614677b57e63b777fbc709ff8634de9726490c4bbb38b6f" :answer-field/choices ["q-79953/selection/29ae03a9f761d292abc2b5d20a15cc24e1ef327068213c1dd84fce3312e3b7eb" "q-79953/selection/737b3859a1677c2f6ae68e264efcac758d99acb897ef54b6b3acffe10b8cc375" "q-79953/selection/eeead72e2dd6a2e09614677b57e63b777fbc709ff8634de9726490c4bbb38b6f" "q-79953/selection/537de86f0ed48c4ed4b80f03e49ca3bf9e07200cc99d1325a778ee3c52e95a9b" "q-79953/selection/e4f339ecf183451e92410984586abe05eb379f62474adfa47a4381e3cf60f2aa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79953" :question/id #uuid "ccde4c95-95fb-5b56-b2d8-f566e370bb5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-79953" :question/problem "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=0$, in ascending powers of $x$ up to and including the term in ${x}^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=1+2x+xy,\\,y(0)=-1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=0$:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(0),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{′}(0),$  ${y}^{″}(0)$ and ${y}^{(3)}(0).$\n\nWe know that $y(0)=-1,$ so we substitute this into the given equation to find ${y}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(0) & =1+2(0)+(0)y(0) \\\\  & =1+0+0(-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{″}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)=2+y+x{y}^{′}\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{″}(0)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(0) & =2+y(0)+(0){y}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =2+(-1)+(0)(1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate ${y}^{″}(x)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{(3)}(x)={y}^{′}+{y}^{′}+x{y}^{″}=2{y}^{′}+x{y}^{″}\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(0)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(0) & =2{y}^{′}(0)+(0){y}^{″}(0) \\\\  & =2(1)+(0)(1) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯ \\\\  & =-1+x\\cdot 1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\cdot (1)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}\\cdot 2+⋯ \\\\  & =-1+x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79953/selection"] :db/ensure [:questi